<<
/A 852 0 R
/Alt (Diagram comparing single-agent and multi-agent architectures for a Mars rover decision-support benchmark using a synthetic scenario dataset. Single agent uses a large language model for direct recommendations. Multi-agent system includes telemetry, terrain, risk, and mission planner agents moderated by an orchestrator, with both approaches producing structured output containing recommended action, risk level, detected hazards, reasoning, and confidence. Evaluation metrics include decision accuracy, hazard detection precision and recall, latency, token usage, confidence, and statistical comparisons. Task requires recommending one action: proceed, pause, reroute, or request human review.)
/ID (ID.0151)
/K 853 0 R
/P 16 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
